          <span class="finding-title">Subprocess timeout kill only terminates the direct child; a descendant holding piped stdout/stderr can hang the reader threads forever, defeating <code>PUBLISH_TIMEOUT_SECS</code></span>
        </div>
        <p class="locpath"><code>crates/callisto-cli/src/runner.rs:73-124</code></p>
        <div class="body">
          <p><span class="label">What</span>On timeout, only <code>child.kill()</code> + <code>child.wait()</code> runs before joining the reader threads &mdash; killing the direct child doesn't close FDs held by descendants that inherited the same pipes (common for <code>npm publish</code> lifecycle scripts, <code>cargo publish</code>/<code>python -m build</code> spawning linker subprocesses). If a descendant survives, the reader threads block on read forever and <code>run_with_timeout</code> never returns, despite <code>PUBLISH_TIMEOUT_SECS = 300</code> existing specifically to bound this.</p>
