<title>Callisto</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #F6F7F9;
    --surface: #FFFFFF;
    --surface-2: #EEF1F4;
    --ink: #161B22;
    --ink-muted: #5B6572;
    --ink-faint: #8992A0;
    --line: #DFE3E8;
    --accent: #146A96;
    --accent-soft: #DCEEF6;
    --amber: #9A6413;
    --amber-soft: #F7EBD6;
    --good: #1E7A50;
    --good-soft: #DFF1E7;
    --mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", "Cascadia Code", "JetBrains Mono", Consolas, monospace;
    --serif: "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", "Book Antiqua", Georgia, serif;
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
      --bg: #0E1217;
      --surface: #151A21;
      --surface-2: #1B222B;
      --ink: #E7EAEE;
      --ink-muted: #98A2AF;
      --ink-faint: #626D7A;
      --line: #262E38;
      --accent: #6BC0EC;
      --accent-soft: #16303C;
      --amber: #E3B15E;
      --amber-soft: #362A16;
      --good: #7ED4A8;
      --good-soft: #163427;
    }
  }

  :root[data-theme="dark"] {
    --bg: #0E1217;
    --surface: #151A21;
    --surface-2: #1B222B;
    --ink: #E7EAEE;
    --ink-muted: #98A2AF;
    --ink-faint: #626D7A;
    --line: #262E38;
    --accent: #6BC0EC;
    --accent-soft: #16303C;
    --amber: #E3B15E;
    --amber-soft: #362A16;
    --good: #7ED4A8;
    --good-soft: #163427;
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  ::selection { background: var(--accent-soft); }

  .page {
    max-width: 780px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 64px 28px 96px;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .eyebrow .dot {
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--good);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--good-soft);
    flex: none;
  }

  header.hero {
    margin-bottom: 52px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(34px, 6vw, 46px);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 14px 0 10px;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .tagline {
    font-size: 19px;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .stat-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-top: 36px;
  }

  .stat {
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: 18px 16px;
  }

  .stat .num {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-size: 26px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .stat .label {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    margin-top: 6px;
  }

  section {
    margin-top: 56px;
  }

  section > .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    padding-bottom: 12px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  h2 {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0;
  }

  p { margin: 0 0 14px; }
  p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .lede {
    font-size: 17.5px;
    color: var(--ink);
    max-width: 66ch;
  }

  .cap-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .cap {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 16px 18px;
  }

  .cap .cap-title {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .cap .cap-body {
    font-size: 14.5px;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .timeline {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--line);
    margin-left: 4px;
    padding-left: 24px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 28px;
  }

  .tl-item { position: relative; }

  .tl-item::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: -30px;
    top: 6px;
    width: 9px;
    height: 9px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .tl-date {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .tl-title {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 17px;
    margin: 4px 0 6px;
  }

  .tl-body {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: 15.5px;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .tl-body code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .pill-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
    margin-top: 10px;
  }

  .pill {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    padding: 3px 9px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .pill.fixed { background: var(--good-soft); color: var(--good); border-color: transparent; }
  .pill.caught { background: var(--amber-soft); color: var(--amber); border-color: transparent; }

  .callout {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--amber);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 14px 18px;
    margin-top: 18px;
  }

  .callout .callout-label {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--amber);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .callout p { color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 15px; }

  .progress-block {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 22px 24px;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  .progress-head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .progress-head .frac {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .progress-head .frac span { color: var(--ink-faint); font-weight: 400; }

  .bar-track {
    height: 8px;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    border-radius: 999px;
    overflow: hidden;
    display: flex;
  }

  .bar-fill {
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--good), var(--accent));
    border-radius: 999px 0 0 999px;
  }

  .tier-list {
    margin-top: 18px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
  }

  .tier {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: 10px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .tier:first-child { border-top: none; }

  .tier-num {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    width: 18px;
    flex: none;
  }

  .tier-name {
    flex: 1;
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .tier-name .sub {
    display: block;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .tier-status {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    padding: 3px 9px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    flex: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .tier-status.done { background: var(--good-soft); color: var(--good); }
  .tier-status.next { background: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--accent); }
  .tier-status.queued { background: var(--surface-2); color: var(--ink-faint); }

  footer {
    margin-top: 64px;
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .stat-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .cap-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>

<div class="page">

  <header class="hero">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>Field report &mdash; 14 August 2026</div>
    <h1>Callisto</h1>
    <p class="tagline">The fast, crash-safe, polyglot monorepo release engine. Native Rust, replacing Node-based changeset tooling, regex manifest edits, and hand-maintained CI matrices.</p>

    <div class="stat-row">
      <div class="stat"><div class="num">10</div><div class="label">crates</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="num">810+</div><div class="label">tests passing</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="num">168</div><div class="label">commits this week</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="num">12</div><div class="label">fixes shipped today</div></div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section id="what">
    <div class="eyebrow"><h2>What it does</h2></div>
    <p class="lede">Callisto discovers a Cargo / npm / PyPI monorepo's package graph, resolves version bumps from changesets across the dependency DAG, and applies them &mdash; manifests, changelogs, lockfiles, tags, publishes &mdash; without ever touching a file it can't roll back.</p>
    <div class="cap-grid">
      <div class="cap">
        <div class="cap-title">Format-preserving edits</div>
        <div class="cap-body">Manifests are edited via CST (<code style="font-family:var(--mono)">toml_edit</code>, JSON indentation fingerprinting), not regex. Comments, ordering, and whitespace survive every bump.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cap">
        <div class="cap-title">Crash-safe writes</div>
        <div class="cap-body">Every write lands via temp-file-then-atomic-rename. A killed process never leaves a half-written manifest behind.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cap">
        <div class="cap-title">Topological cascades</div>
        <div class="cap-body">A <code style="font-family:var(--mono)">petgraph</code> DAG with Tarjan SCC detection computes cascading bumps across the whole workspace and catches circular dependencies before they ship.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cap">
        <div class="cap-title">Zero-config CI matrices</div>
        <div class="cap-body"><code style="font-family:var(--mono)">callisto matrix</code> reads napi-rs and maturin native targets straight from manifests &mdash; one source of truth instead of hand-maintained YAML.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="week">
    <div class="eyebrow"><h2>This week</h2></div>
    <div class="timeline">

      <div class="tl-item">
        <div class="tl-date">Aug 8</div>
        <div class="tl-title">Foundation hardening</div>
        <div class="tl-body">Decoupled <code>callisto-conventional</code> from the VCS layer, fixed a workspace-inherited-version overwrite bug, closed a shell-injection hole in the CI action, and taught publish to detect the right package manager (pnpm / yarn / bun / npm) automatically.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="tl-item">
        <div class="tl-date">Aug 11&ndash;12</div>
        <div class="tl-title">Shipped <code>callisto matrix</code></div>
        <div class="tl-body">A flagship feature built end to end in two days: native build target auto-discovery for napi-rs and maturin, runtime-version constraints, CLI surface, and CI wiring &mdash; 24 commits, full spec-to-implementation cycle.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="tl-item">
        <div class="tl-date">Aug 12</div>
        <div class="tl-title">Full workspace audit</div>
        <div class="tl-body">24-agent adversarial sweep across architecture, security, performance, and correctness. Found and fixed 8 confirmed critical/high bugs same-day, including a version parser that crashed on this repo's own <code>version.workspace = true</code> crates, a silent no-op in NuGet/GitHub Release publishing, and a path-traversal write via an unvalidated changelog config path.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="tl-item">
        <div class="tl-date">Aug 13</div>
        <div class="tl-title">Manifest write performance, done properly</div>
        <div class="tl-body">Two specs, both through full adversarial spec and plan review before a line was written: splitting manifest mutation from disk persistence, then batching same-file writes so a cascade touching one <code>Cargo.toml</code> five times opens, mutates, and persists it once instead of five.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="tl-item">
        <div class="tl-date">Aug 14 &mdash; today</div>
        <div class="tl-title">Re-audit and backlog sweep</div>
        <div class="tl-body">Re-verified all previously-deferred audit findings against current code with four parallel agents &mdash; several had already been fixed or partially fixed without being logged. Built a clean, priority-ordered backlog of 31 items and shipped the first 12 the same day.</div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="today">
    <div class="eyebrow"><h2>Today, in detail</h2></div>
    <p class="lede">Twelve fixes, each independently reviewed before it landed. Three were genuine security holes; the rest closed silent-failure and type-safety gaps. The review step itself caught two real bugs before they shipped.</p>

    <div class="callout">
      <div class="callout-label">Caught by review, not by the original fix</div>
      <p>The tag-name injection fix was reviewed by a second pass that traced a sibling code path and found tag names read back from the repository itself &mdash; not just ones Callisto renders &mdash; flowed unguarded into shelled <code style="font-family:var(--mono)">git diff</code>/<code style="font-family:var(--mono)">git log</code> calls. Same class of bug, different door. Closed in the same commit.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout">
      <div class="callout-label">Caught by review, not by the original fix</div>
      <p>A secret-redaction fix for subprocess stderr had a URL-parsing heuristic that <em>looked</em> right but silently failed to redact a credential when the password itself contained a <code style="font-family:var(--mono)">/</code> or a second <code style="font-family:var(--mono)">@</code> &mdash; exactly the shape a base64 token takes. Rewritten to fail toward over-redaction instead of under-redaction.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="pill-row">
      <span class="pill fixed">git tag CLI injection</span>
      <span class="pill fixed">credential leak in error logs</span>
      <span class="pill fixed">subprocess memory-exhaustion DoS</span>
      <span class="pill fixed">silent no-op on malformed manifests</span>
      <span class="pill fixed">401/403 false-positive misclassification</span>
      <span class="pill fixed">napi Linux target never resolved</span>
      <span class="pill fixed">PEP 503 name mismatch on cascades</span>
      <span class="pill fixed">duplicate CI matrix jobs</span>
      <span class="pill caught">unscoped npm package silently dropped explicit public access</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="next">
    <div class="eyebrow"><h2>What's next</h2></div>
    <p class="lede">Nineteen items left in the backlog, grouped into five phases and sequenced by risk. Same bar for all of them: red test, independent review, full suite green, before anything is called done.</p>

    <div class="progress-block">
      <div class="progress-head">
        <span>Backlog</span>
        <span class="frac">12<span>/31</span></span>
      </div>
      <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width: 38.7%; height: 100%;"></div></div>

      <div class="tier-list">
        <div class="tier">
          <div class="tier-num">01</div>
          <div class="tier-name">Architecture<span class="sub">Dedupe identity resolution, quiet subprocess probes, drop an unused AGPL dev-dependency</span></div>
          <div class="tier-status next">in progress</div>
        </div>
        <div class="tier">
          <div class="tier-num">02</div>
          <div class="tier-name">Performance<span class="sub">Share one git handle across plan-publish, stop double-parsing manifests in the matrix command</span></div>
          <div class="tier-status queued">queued</div>
        </div>
        <div class="tier">
          <div class="tier-num">03</div>
          <div class="tier-name">Dependency hygiene<span class="sub">Fix a real Unix path bug, centralize re-pinned versions, drop dead weight</span></div>
          <div class="tier-status queued">queued</div>
        </div>
        <div class="tier">
          <div class="tier-num">04</div>
          <div class="tier-name">Documentation<span class="sub">Write up <code style="font-family:var(--mono)">callisto matrix</code> properly, correct two factual errors in the architecture doc</span></div>
          <div class="tier-status queued">queued</div>
        </div>
        <div class="tier">
          <div class="tier-num">05</div>
          <div class="tier-name">Findings from this week's reviews<span class="sub">Extend credential redaction to git subprocess errors; wire up native-target drift detection end to end</span></div>
          <div class="tier-status queued">queued</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <span>unsafe_code = forbid, workspace-wide</span>
    <span>every commit: red test &rarr; independent review &rarr; green suite</span>
  </footer>

</div>

