      "criterion": "The malformed/edge-case membership-declaration group (AC-09, AC-09b, AC-09c, AC-09d, AC-09e, AC-09f, AC-09g, AC-09h, AC-09i, AC-10, AC-11, AC-11b, AC-11d) ships with at least one regression test per criterion using these exact fixtures: a workspace root Cargo.toml with `[workspace]\\nmembers = \"crates/*\"` (bare string, not an array) that toml_edit parses successfully as a document, plus tools/outside/Cargo.toml containing a valid [package] table at a path that does not match the literal glob pattern crates/* (asserting AC-09's fall-back-to-absent-filter behavior: tools/outside is returned, proving every candidate is admitted rather than the malformed field being treated as a literal single-entry glob list, and that projects() does not panic); a workspace root Cargo.toml with `[workspace]\\nmembers = [\"crates/*\"]\\nexclude = \"crates/scratch-example\"` (well-formed members, bare-string exclude), plus crates/scratch-example/Cargo.toml, crates/kept-example/Cargo.toml, and tools/outside/Cargo.toml, each containing a valid [package] table (asserting AC-09b's exclude-alone-falls-back-to-absent, members-still-applies behavior: crates/scratch-example and crates/kept-example are both returned because the malformed exclude excludes nothing, and tools/outside is not returned because the well-formed members filter still applies); a root package.json with `\"workspaces\": \"packages/*\"` (bare string, not an array), plus tools/outside/package.json containing a valid \"name\" field at a path that does not match the literal glob pattern packages/* (asserting AC-09c's fall-back-to-absent-npm-filter behavior: tools/outside is returned, proving every candidate is admitted rather than the malformed field being treated as a literal single-entry glob); a workspace root Cargo.toml whose content is not syntactically valid TOML at all, e.g. `[workspace\\nmembers = [` with no closing bracket or brace, such that content.parse::<toml_edit::DocumentMut>() returns Err, plus crates/kept/Cargo.toml elsewhere in the tree containing a valid [package] table (asserting AC-09d's fall-back-to-absent-Cargo-filter behavior: crates/kept is returned, proving the walk continues and admits candidates rather than merely not panicking; no-panic, no-whole-walk-error behavior, distinct from AC-09's well-formed-TOML-wrong-shape case); a root package.json whose content is not syntactically valid JSON at all, e.g. a trailing comma after the last object member, such that serde_json::from_str::<serde_json::Value>(&content) returns Err, plus packages/kept/package.json elsewhere in the tree containing a valid \"name\" field (asserting AC-09e's fall-back-to-absent-npm-filter behavior: packages/kept is returned, proving the walk continues and admits candidates rather than merely not panicking; no-panic, no-whole-walk-error behavior, distinct from AC-09c's well-formed-JSON-malformed-workspaces-field case); a workspace root Cargo.toml with `members = [\"crates/kept-example\", \"crates/[unterminated\"]` (one well-formed glob, one glob string globset::GlobBuilder fails to compile) plus crates/kept-example/Cargo.toml containing a valid [package] table (asserting AC-09f's narrowest-scope-degradation behavior: crates/kept-example is included, and the invalid glob entry does not panic, error the walk, or disable the whole members list); a root package.json declaring `{\"workspaces\": [\"packages/kept-example\", \"packages/[unterminated\"]}` (one well-formed glob, one glob string globset::GlobBuilder fails to compile) plus packages/kept-example/package.json containing a valid \"name\" field (asserting AC-09g's narrowest-scope-degradation behavior for the npm case: packages/kept-example is included, and the invalid glob entry does not panic, error the walk, or disable the whole workspaces list); a pnpm-workspace.yaml declaring `packages:\\n  - \"packages/kept-example\"\\n  - \"packages/[unterminated\"` (one well-formed glob, one glob string globset::GlobBuilder fails to compile) plus packages/kept-example/package.json containing a valid \"name\" field (asserting AC-09h's narrowest-scope-degradation behavior for the pnpm case: packages/kept-example is included, and the invalid glob entry does not panic, error the walk, or disable the whole packages list); a workspace root Cargo.toml with members = [\"crates/*\"] and exclude = [\"crates/scratch-example\", \"crates/[unterminated\"] (one well-formed exclude glob, one glob string globset::GlobBuilder fails to compile) plus crates/scratch-example/Cargo.toml and crates/kept-example/Cargo.toml both containing a valid [package] table (asserting AC-09i's narrowest-scope-degradation behavior for Cargo's exclude list specifically: crates/scratch-example is excluded, crates/kept-example is included, and the invalid exclude entry does not panic, error the walk, or disable the whole exclude list); a root package.json with `\"workspaces\": []` (present, empty array) alongside at least one other package.json elsewhere in the tree (asserting AC-10's zero-Npm-entries behavior, distinguishing empty-array from missing-field); a pnpm-workspace.yaml containing the literal malformed content `packages: [\"packages/*\"` (unterminated flow sequence) such that yaml_rust2::YamlLoader::load_from_str returns Err(..), with no package.json \"workspaces\" field present at the same root, plus packages/kept/package.json elsewhere in the tree containing a valid \"name\" field (asserting AC-11's fall-back-to-absent-filter behavior: packages/kept is returned, proving the npm filter is treated as absent rather than admit-nothing; no-panic, no-whole-walk-error behavior); a pnpm-workspace.yaml containing the literal well-formed-YAML-but-wrong-shape content `packages: \"packages/*\"` (a bare string value for packages:, valid YAML that parses successfully but is not a sequence), plus packages/kept/package.json elsewhere in the tree containing a valid \"name\" field (asserting AC-11b's schema-mismatch fall-back-to-absent-filter behavior: packages/kept is returned, proving the npm filter is treated as absent rather than admit-nothing; no-panic behavior); and a pnpm-workspace.yaml containing only the literal content `# no packages here\\n` (a comments-only file, for which yaml_rust2::YamlLoader::load_from_str returns Ok(vec![]) — a successful parse producing zero YAML documents, not an Err and not a single wrong-shaped document), plus packages/kept/package.json elsewhere in the tree containing a valid \"name\" field (asserting AC-11d's fall-back-to-absent-filter behavior: packages/kept is returned, proving the npm filter is treated as absent rather than admit-nothing; no-panic behavior — the implementation must not unconditionally index docs[0] or call docs.first().unwrap() on the resulting empty Vec<Yaml>).",
